  "worked_solution": "To plot $x=2{y}^{2}+3y,$ we will first plot the function $y=2{x}^{2}+3x$ and then reflect it over the line $y=x.$\n\nThe curve $y=2{x}^{2}+3x$ is a parabola. It has the following factored form:\n\n$$\ny=x(2x+3)\n$$\n\nFrom the factored form above, we get the following graph:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240562/assets/c1b824ff56cc67a930cc5777aed40f913371154631b7caa2a288b5ce7a64a60b.png)\n\nNow, to get the curve $x=2{y}^{2}+3y,$ we just have to reflect the curve $y=2{x}^{2}+3x$ over the line $y=x,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240562/assets/658ed684c36124ca72a172050f5587e51f8eb9c7395bc6aa2fbe1eea09aa7c63.png)",
